From 7cfcd31600f2b50a32f43dec46013bf4a1ff5261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <backcountrymountains@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:34:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add a "Dolby Vision files" setting: DV decoder or
 HDR10/HDR10+ base layer

On a TV without Dolby Vision the device's DV engine renders DV to plain
HDR10, which drops any HDR10+ metadata in hybrid files. Let the user
choose how DV files are decoded:

- Dolby Vision decoder (default, unchanged behaviour)
- Base layer on the HEVC decoder, keeping HDR10+
- Base layer as plain HDR10, with the HDR10+ SEI messages removed

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
